---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Ayush Mishra | Computer Scientist & AI Researcher">
  <!-- Concise Bio Section (Chip Huyen style) -->
  <section id="about" class="intro-bio home-hero-bio">
    <div class="profile-container">
      <a href="https://github.com/ayush190511" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="profile-img-link" title="Ayush Mishra">
        <img src="/assets/logo2.jpeg" alt="Ayush Mishra" class="profile-img" />
      </a>
      <div class="profile-pill-badge">
        <span class="status-dot"></span>
        <span>Bengaluru, India</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>
      I’m <strong>Ayush Mishra</strong>, a Computer Scientist and AI Researcher based in Bengaluru, India. My research centers on <strong>Multimodal Deep Learning</strong>, <strong>Vision Transformers</strong>, and <strong>High-Performance Machine Learning Systems</strong>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Currently, I serve as an <strong>Academic Researcher &amp; Faculty Mentor</strong> at <a href="https://www.dsce.edu.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Dayananda Sagar College of Engineering (DSCE), Bengaluru</strong></a>, mentoring engineering students and guiding applied research in deep learning.
    </p>

    <p>
      I earned my <strong>M.Tech in CSE (Data Science)</strong> from <a href="https://www.svnit.ac.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>SVNIT Surat</strong></a> (CGPA 8.42/10). My master’s thesis introduced a novel Cross-Modal Gated Fusion architecture accepted &amp; presented at <a href="/research"><strong>IC2NS2 '26</strong></a> (forthcoming Dec 2026), achieving <strong>96.66% SOTA accuracy</strong> on multimodal benchmarks.
    </p>

    <p>
      In addition to academic research, I design production AI systems spanning automated MLOps pipelines (DVC, MLflow, Docker, AWS), low-latency inference services, and live platforms like <a href="https://allagecalculator.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>AllAgeCalculator.com</strong></a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
